{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>and the Pathrusim, and the Casluhim, from where the Philistines went forth.</b> Scripture informs you that this nation of the Philistines were of mixed stock, for the Pathrusim and the Casluhim would exchange their wives with one another, and from them the Philistimes emerged. And you will find that all these genealogies of Egypt — their names are after their end: they were lost in the sea; and the firstborn was called Ludim because they were born and drowned in the sea."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:32.140564369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}